<title>ITALY: SOCCER-ITALIAN FIRST DIVISION SCORERS.</title>
<headline>SOCCER-ITALIAN FIRST DIVISION SCORERS.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1997-02-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Leading scorers in Italian first</p>
<p>division after matches on Sunday:</p>
<p>15 - Filippo Inzaghi (Atalanta)</p>
<p>14 - Abel Balbo (Roma)</p>
<p>13 - Roberto Mancini and Vincenzo Montella (both Sampdoria)</p>
<p>12 - Marcelo Otero (Vicenza)</p>
<p>10 - Gabriel Batistuta (Fiorentina), Youri Djorkaeff (Inter),</p>
<p>Giuseppe Signori (Lazio)</p>
<p>9 - George Weah (Milan)</p>
<p>8 - Enrico Chiesa (Parma), Pasquale Luiso (Piacenza)</p>
<p>7 - Oliver Bierhoff and Paolo Poggi (both Udinese), Alessandro</p>
<p>Del Piero and Michele Padovano (both Juventus)</p>
<p>6 - Alfredo Aglietti (Napoli), Marco Amoroso (Udinese), Igor</p>
<p>Kolyvanov (Bologna), Luis Oliveira (Fiorentina), Sandro</p>
<p>Tovalieri (Cagliari)</p>
<p>5 - Demetrio Albertini (Milan), Nicola Caccia and Andre Cruz</p>
<p>(both  Napoli), Marco Carparelli (Sampdoria), Filippo Maniero</p>
<p>(Verona), Roberto Murgita (Vicenza), Marco Negri (Perugia),</p>
<p>Anselmo Robbiati (Fiorentina)</p>
</text>
